WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.432
Now we move from text to temporal data.

00:00:03.432 --> 00:00:06.192
The first decision is the data type.

00:00:06.192 --> 00:00:08.697
DATE represents a calendar date.

00:00:08.697 --> 00:00:14.287
TIMESTAMP represents a date and clock time without time-zone interpretation.

00:00:14.287 --> 00:00:17.752
TIMESTAMPTZ represents an instant in time.

00:00:17.752 --> 00:00:19.512
INTERVAL represents a duration.

00:00:19.512 --> 00:00:25.252
Choosing the correct type is more important than choosing a formatting function.

00:00:25.252 --> 00:00:29.927
Choose temporal types based on meaning.

00:00:29.927 --> 00:00:32.727
DATE is for calendar dates without time of day.

00:00:32.727 --> 00:00:39.852
TIMESTAMP stores a date and time without a time-zone interpretation.

00:00:39.852 --> 00:00:45.042
TIMESTAMPTZ represents an instant in time and is usually safer for events that cross regions or

00:00:45.042 --> 00:00:47.511
daylight-saving changes.
